    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nOxygen-Hemoglobin dissociation dynamics: Right shift (Bohr effect = decreased Hb affinity, enhances O2 release to tissues): increased H+ / decreased pH (acidosis), increased PaCO2, increased temperature, increased 2,3-DPG. Left shift (increased Hb affinity, holds O2 tighter): alkalosis, hypothermia, decreased 2,3-DPG, Fetal hemoglobin (HbF), and Carbon Monoxide (CO).",
