    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nMechanisms of host immunity: 1) Innate/Non-specific immunity: primary anatomical barriers (skin, gastric acid pH 1-3), phagocytic cells (neutrophils, macrophages). 2) Adaptive/Specific immunity: Humoral immunity (B-lymphocytes bind antigen epitopes, endocytosis, antigen processing and presentation on MHC Class II to CD4+ helper T-cells). Activated CD4+ T-cells release interleukins to trigger B-cell clonal expansion and differentiation into antibody-secreting plasma cells and memory B-cells.",
