    "leaneNotes": "Dr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Key lecture pearls, high-yield highlighted terms, and memory aids noted during DMF comprehensive board coaching.",
    "summary": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nHypersensitivity classification (Gell and Coombs): Type I (Immediate/Anaphylactic, IgE-mediated, mast cell histamine release; e.g. asthma, anaphylaxis, penicillin allergy). Type II (Cytotoxic, IgG/IgM, complement activation; e.g. erythroblastosis fetalis, rheumatic fever, Goodpasture). Type III (Immune Complex, antigen-antibody deposition; e.g. SLE, serum sickness). Type IV (Delayed/Cell-Mediated, T-cells/macrophages; e.g. tuberculin PPD, contact dermatitis). Tissue repair capacity: Labile cells (continuous division, skin/oral mucosa), Stable cells (quiescent but can divide, liver/renal tubules), Permanent cells (cannot divide, cardiac muscle/neurons).\n\nAI Conceptual Breakdown:\nThis page covers essential clinical and scientific concepts of Immunopathology: Hypersensitivity Reactions (Types I-IV) & Tissue Repair. Understanding these foundational principles allows rapid recognition of Board examination question stems and clinical diagnostic dilemmas.\n\nPRC Board Examination Pearl:\nFocus on high-yield hallmarks, diagnostic criteria, and standard clinical dosages/classifications associated with Immunopathology: Hypersensitivity Reactions (Types I-IV) & Tissue Repair.\n\nDr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Key lecture pearls, high-yield highlighted terms, and memory aids noted during DMF comprehensive board coaching.",
