    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nStreptococcal microbiology and oral colonizers: Blood agar hemolysis: 1) Alpha-hemolytic (partial/greenish hemolysis): S. pneumoniae (optochin sensitive, capsule), S. viridans group (optochin resistant; S. mutans [primary etiological agent of dental caries via dextran production from sucrose], S. sanguinis [first colonizer of dental pellicle, risk for subacute bacterial endocarditis on damaged heart valves], S. salivarius [primary colonizer of tongue surface 10-12 hours after birth]). 2) Beta-hemolytic (complete clear hemolysis zone): Group A Streptococcus (GAS: S. pyogenes; causes pharyngitis, scarlet fever, rheumatic fever, glomerulonephritis), Group B (S. agalactiae; neonatal sepsis/meningitis). 3) Gamma-hemolytic (non-hemolytic; Enterococcus faecalis).",
