    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nPathogenic Gram-negative cocci & spirochetes: 1) Neisseria: Gram-negative diplococci ('kidney-bean' shaped), oxidase-positive, grow on Thayer-Martin/chocolate agar. N. gonorrhoeae causes gonorrhea and neonatal ophthalmia neonatorum; N. meningitidis causes epidemic bacterial meningitis and Waterhouse-Friderichsen syndrome. 2) Treponema pallidum (Syphilis): Motile spirochete visualized by darkfield microscopy. Primary Syphilis (Hard painless Chancre at site of inoculation, highly infectious, heals spontaneously in 3-6 weeks). Secondary Syphilis (Maculopapular rash on palms/soles, oral mucous patches, Condyloma lata, generalized lymphadenopathy). Tertiary Syphilis (Gummatous necrosis of palate/tongue, tabes dorsalis, cardiovascular syphilitic aortitis). Congenital Syphilis: Hutchinson's triad (Hutchinson incisors/mulberry molars, interstitial keratitis, eighth nerve deafness).",
