    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nAcid-fast bacilli & virology principles: 1) Mycobacterium leprae (Hansen's disease): Acid-fast bacillus with predilection for cool peripheral tissues (skin, superficial nerves, nasal mucosa). Tuberculoid leprosy (high cell-mediated immunity, few hypopigmented anesthetic skin lesions, nerve thickening). Lepromatous leprosy (depressed CMI, diffuse infiltrate, 'leonine facies', loss of eyebrows/eyelashes, saddlenose deformity, extensive peripheral neuropathy). 2) Virology fundamentals: Viruses are obligate intracellular parasites containing either DNA or RNA (never both!). Virion structure: Nucleic acid core surrounded by protein capsid (together = nucleocapsid); some possess lipid envelope derived from host membrane.",
    "aiUnderstanding": "AI Conceptual Breakdown:\nThis page covers essential clinical and scientific concepts of Mycobacteriology: Leprosy (Hansen's Disease) & Viral Architecture Fundamentals. Understanding these foundational principles allows rapid recognition of Board examination question stems and clinical diagnostic dilemmas.",
