    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nMajor DNA virus families: 1) Herpesviridae (enveloped dsDNA, establish latency): HSV-1 (oral herpes, primary herpetic gingivostomatitis, trigeminal ganglion latency), HSV-2 (genital herpes, sacral ganglion latency), VZV (chickenpox/herpes zoster, dorsal root ganglion latency), EBV (infectious mononucleosis, Burkitt lymphoma, hairy leukoplakia), CMV (owl's eye nuclear inclusions), HHV-8 (Kaposi's sarcoma in HIV). 2) Papillomaviridae: HPV types 6 & 11 (condyloma acuminata, benign squamous papilloma), HPV types 16 & 18 (cervical carcinoma and oropharyngeal squamous cell carcinoma). 3) Poxviridae: Smallpox (Variola; largest virus, intracytoplasmic Guarnieri inclusion bodies). 4) Hepadnaviridae: Hepatitis B Virus (HBV; enveloped partially double-stranded circular DNA virus with reverse transcriptase; Dane particle; HBsAg indicates current infection).",
