    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nArboviruses & Lentivirus pathology: 1) Flaviviruses (mosquito-borne, Aedes aegypti): Dengue virus (breakbone fever, leukopenia, thrombocytopenia, capillary fragility, Tourniquet test positive). Yellow fever virus (hepatotropic and nephrotropic; causes jaundice, black vomit, liver Councilman inclusion bodies). Zika virus (congenital microcephaly and fetal brain abnormalities; associated with Guillain-Barr\u00e9 syndrome). 2) Retroviridae (Lentivirus): Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV): enveloped positive-sense ssRNA with reverse transcriptase (converts viral RNA to proviral DNA). Targets CD4+ T-lymphocytes and macrophages using gp120 (binding to CD4 and CXCR4/CCR5 co-receptors) and gp41 (fusion). AIDS defined when CD4 count falls below 200 cells/uL; oral hallmarks include oral candidiasis, hairy leukoplakia (EBV), Kaposi's sarcoma (HHV-8), and necrotizing ulcerative periodontitis.",
