    "leaneNotes": "Dr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Key lecture pearls, high-yield highlighted terms, and memory aids noted during DMF comprehensive board coaching.",
    "summary": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nParasitic infections & ischemic heart disease: 1) Opportunistic protozoal pathogens: Pneumocystis jirovecii (formerly P. carinii; opportunistic interstitial plasma cell pneumonia in AIDS); Trichomonas vaginalis (flagellated protozoan causing vaginitis with frothy green discharge and strawberry cervix). 2) Coronary Artery Disease (CAD): Atherosclerosis is the primary underlying cause. Pathogenesis: endothelial injury -> LDL oxidation -> macrophage uptake forming foam cells -> fatty streak -> fibrous plaque (atheroma) encroaching arterial lumen -> fibrous cap rupture with superimposed thrombosis. Stable angina (chest pain on exertion relieved by rest or nitroglycerin), Unstable angina (pain at rest, pre-infarction), Myocardial Infarction (coagulative necrosis of myocardium, ST-elevation, elevated Troponin I and CK-MB).\n\nAI Conceptual Breakdown:\nThis page covers essential clinical and scientific concepts of Parasitology & Cardiovascular Pathology: Coronary Artery Disease & Atherosclerosis. Understanding these foundational principles allows rapid recognition of Board examination question stems and clinical diagnostic dilemmas.\n\nPRC Board Examination Pearl:\nFocus on high-yield hallmarks, diagnostic criteria, and standard clinical dosages/classifications associated with Parasitology & Cardiovascular Pathology: Coronary Artery Disease & Atherosclerosis.\n\nDr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Key lecture pearls, high-yield highlighted terms, and memory aids noted during DMF comprehensive board coaching.",
