    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nLocal anesthetic pharmacology: Reversibly bind to specific receptors inside voltage-gated sodium channels on the inner nerve axolemma, blocking sodium influx and action potential propagation. The uncharged lipophilic free base (RN) crosses the nerve sheath; the charged cationic form (RNH+) binds the intracellular channel receptor. In tissue inflammation (acidic pH < 6.0), more drug exists in the ionized RNH+ form, failing to penetrate nerve membranes and causing anesthesia failure!",
