    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nAmides vs Esters differentiation: Amides have two 'i's in their generic name (Lidocaine, Mepivacaine, Prilocaine, Articaine, Bupivacaine); Esters have only one 'i' (Procaine, Tetracaine, Benzocaine, Cocaine). Esters metabolized in plasma by pseudocholinesterase to PABA (responsible for frequent allergic reactions); Amides metabolized primarily in liver by CYP450 (true allergy to amides is extremely rare). Articaine possesses an ester side chain, enabling 90% plasma hydrolysis and superior safety.",
    "aiUnderstanding": "AI Conceptual Breakdown:\nThis page covers essential clinical and scientific concepts of Dental Pharmacology: Chemical Classes of Local Anesthetics (Amides vs Esters). Understanding these foundational principles allows rapid recognition of Board examination question stems and clinical diagnostic dilemmas.",
