    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nTherapeutic safety metrics: Therapeutic Index (TI) = LD50 / ED50 (or TD50 / ED50). A higher TI represents a wide margin of safety. Drugs with narrow therapeutic indices (Digoxin, Warfarin, Lithium, Theophylline, Phenytoin) require tight therapeutic monitoring. Crucial clinical rule: Doubling the dose does NOT double the clinical effect; it increases duration and toxicity exponentially!",
