    "summary": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nTherapeutic safety metrics: Therapeutic Index (TI) = LD50 / ED50 (or TD50 / ED50). A higher TI represents a wide margin of safety. Drugs with narrow therapeutic indices (Digoxin, Warfarin, Lithium, Theophylline, Phenytoin) require tight therapeutic monitoring. Crucial clinical rule: Doubling the dose does NOT double the clinical effect; it increases duration and toxicity exponentially!\n\nAI Conceptual Breakdown:\nThis page covers essential clinical and scientific concepts of Pharmacology Principles: Therapeutic Index & Drug Safety Margins. Understanding these foundational principles allows rapid recognition of Board examination question stems and clinical diagnostic dilemmas.\n\nPRC Board Examination Pearl:\nFocus on high-yield hallmarks, diagnostic criteria, and standard clinical dosages/classifications associated with Pharmacology Principles: Therapeutic Index & Drug Safety Margins.\n\nDr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Key lecture pearls, high-yield highlighted terms, and memory aids noted during DMF comprehensive board coaching.",
