    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nSedative-hypnotics: Benzodiazepines (Diazepam, Midazolam, Triazolam) enhance GABA-A receptor action by increasing the FREQUENCY of chloride channel opening, producing sedation, anxiolysis, muscle relaxation, and anterograde amnesia. High safety ceiling; reversed by Flumazenil. Barbiturates (Phenobarbital, Thiopental) increase the DURATION of chloride channel opening and can open channels directly at high doses, carrying severe risk of fatal respiratory depression.",
