    "summary": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nAnesthetic math for 1.8 mL standard dental cartridge: Percentage x 10 x 1.8 mL = total mg per carpule. 1) 2% Lidocaine = 20 mg/mL x 1.8 = 36 mg/carpule. 2) 3% Mepivacaine = 30 mg/mL x 1.8 = 54 mg/carpule. 3) 4% Articaine = 40 mg/mL x 1.8 = 72 mg/carpule. 4) 0.5% Bupivacaine = 5 mg/mL x 1.8 = 9 mg/carpule. Vasoconstrictor math: 1:100,000 epinephrine contains 0.01 mg/mL = 0.018 mg epi per carpule; 1:200,000 contains 0.009 mg epi per carpule.\n\nAI Conceptual Breakdown:\nThis page covers essential clinical and scientific concepts of Local Anesthesia: Cartridge Volume & Milligram Calculations. Understanding these foundational principles allows rapid recognition of Board examination question stems and clinical diagnostic dilemmas.\n\nPRC Board Examination Pearl:\nFocus on high-yield hallmarks, diagnostic criteria, and standard clinical dosages/classifications associated with Local Anesthesia: Cartridge Volume & Milligram Calculations.\n\nDr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Key lecture pearls, high-yield highlighted terms, and memory aids noted during DMF comprehensive board coaching.",
