    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nMalamed Board MRDs for dental local anesthetics: 1) Lidocaine (with epi): 7.0 mg/kg (3.2 mg/lb), absolute max = 500 mg (~13.8 carpules). 2) Mepivacaine 3% plain: 6.6 mg/kg (3.0 mg/lb), absolute max = 400 mg (~7.4 carpules). 3) Articaine 4%: 7.0 mg/kg (3.2 mg/lb), absolute max = 500 mg (~6.9 carpules). 4) Bupivacaine 0.5%: 2.0 mg/kg (0.9 mg/lb), absolute max = 90 mg (~10 carpules). 5) Prilocaine 4%: 8.0 mg/kg (3.6 mg/lb), absolute max = 600 mg (~8.3 carpules; risk of methemoglobinemia).",
