    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nVasoconstrictor dosing rules: Healthy patient (ASA I): Maximum Epinephrine = 0.2 mg per appointment (~11 carpules of 1:100,000). Cardiac patient (ASA III/IV, ischemic heart disease, hypertension): Maximum Epinephrine = 0.04 mg (~2 carpules of 1:100,000 or ~4 carpules of 1:200,000). Absolute contraindications: uncontrolled hypertension, unstable angina, recent MI <6 months, refractory arrhythmias, pheochromocytoma, non-selective beta-blockers (Propranolol: severe hypertensive crisis risk), TCAs.",
