    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nLocal Anesthetic Systemic Toxicity (LAST) clinical stages: 1) Initial CNS excitation: circumoral numbness, tongue paresthesia, metallic taste, tinnitus, slurred speech, shivering, muscle twitching, generalized tonic-clonic convulsions. 2) Secondary CNS depression: unconsciousness, respiratory arrest. 3) Cardiovascular collapse: bradycardia, severe hypotension, ventricular fibrillation, asystole. Emergency protocol: Stop injection, call 911, hyperventilate with 100% O2, Midazolam for seizures, administer 20% Lipid Emulsion (Intralipid).",
