    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nNon-opioid pain therapeutics: NSAIDs (Ibuprofen, Naproxen, Ketorolac) inhibit COX-1 and COX-2 enzymes to block prostaglandin synthesis; provide analgesic, anti-inflammatory, and antipyretic actions; side effects include GI ulceration, bleeding, renal impairment. Acetaminophen (Paracetamol) acts centrally to provide analgesia and antipyresis with NO peripheral anti-inflammatory action; maximum dose 3-4 g/day; overdose causes fatal hepatic necrosis via toxic metabolite NAPQI (antidote: N-acetylcysteine / NAC).",
    "aiUnderstanding": "AI Conceptual Breakdown:\nThis page covers essential clinical and scientific concepts of Dental Pharmacology: Non-Opioid Analgesics (NSAIDs & Acetaminophen). Understanding these foundational principles allows rapid recognition of Board examination question stems and clinical diagnostic dilemmas.",
