    "leaneNotes": "Dr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Key lecture pearls, high-yield highlighted terms, and memory aids noted during DMF comprehensive board coaching.",
    "summary": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nOpioid pharmacology: Mu-opioid receptor agonists in CNS (Codeine, Hydrocodone, Oxycodone, Tramadol, Morphine). Therapeutic effects: analgesia, sedation, euphoria, antitussive. Adverse effects: respiratory depression (cause of death), constipation, nausea, physical dependence. Pathognomonic triad of opioid overdose: CNS depression/coma, respiratory depression, and pinpoint pupils (miosis; tolerance never develops to miosis or constipation!). Specific competitive antagonist: Naloxone (Narcan).\n\nAI Conceptual Breakdown:\nThis page covers essential clinical and scientific concepts of Dental Pharmacology: Opioid Analgesics & Overdose Reversal. Understanding these foundational principles allows rapid recognition of Board examination question stems and clinical diagnostic dilemmas.\n\nPRC Board Examination Pearl:\nFocus on high-yield hallmarks, diagnostic criteria, and standard clinical dosages/classifications associated with Dental Pharmacology: Opioid Analgesics & Overdose Reversal.\n\nDr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Key lecture pearls, high-yield highlighted terms, and memory aids noted during DMF comprehensive board coaching.",
