    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nBeta-lactam antibiotics: Bactericidal mechanism inhibiting bacterial cell wall synthesis by binding Penicillin-Binding Proteins (PBPs) and blocking peptidoglycan cross-linking. Amoxicillin: drug of choice for odontogenic infections and infective endocarditis prophylaxis. Augmentin (Amoxicillin + Clavulanic acid): clavulanate irreversibly inhibits beta-lactamase (penicillinase) enzymes. Cephalosporins have 1-5% cross-allergenicity with penicillins.",
