    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nNon-beta-lactams: Macrolides (Azithromycin, Clarithromycin) inhibit 50S ribosomes, bacteriostatic, excellent for penicillin allergy. Clindamycin inhibits 50S ribosomes, penetrates bone well, but carries highest risk of C. difficile colitis. Metronidazole (Flagyl) breaks anaerobic DNA, creates severe Disulfiram-like reaction with alcohol. Tetracyclines (Doxycycline) bind 30S ribosomes, chelate calcium causing intrinsic tooth staining in children under 8.",
