    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nAHA Antibiotic Prophylaxis indications: 1) Prosthetic cardiac valves or valve repairs, 2) Previous history of infective endocarditis, 3) Congenital heart disease (unrepaired cyanotic CHD, repaired with prosthesis for first 6 months, repaired with residual defect), 4) Cardiac transplant recipients with valvulopathy. Standard regimen: Amoxicillin 2.0 g orally 30-60 min prior (peds: 50 mg/kg). Penicillin allergy: Cephalexin 2.0 g or Azithromycin 500 mg (peds: 15 mg/kg).",
