    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nMedical emergencies in dental office: Vasovagal Syncope (most common dental emergency; management: Trendelenburg position, loosen tight clothing, oxygen). Angina Pectoris (substernal chest pain; management: sit upright, sublingual Nitroglycerin 0.4mg every 5 min up to 3 doses; CONTRAINDICATED with PDE-5 inhibitors like Viagra/Cialis). Myocardial Infarction (pain unrelieved by nitroglycerin; MONA protocol: Morphine, Oxygen, Nitroglycerin, Aspirin 325mg chewed, activate EMS).",
