    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nEndocrine & neurological emergencies: Hypoglycemia (blood glucose <70 mg/dL in diabetic patients; diaphoresis, tachycardia, tremor, confusion). Conscious patient: oral glucose / juice / candy following Rule of 15; Unconscious patient: Glucagon 1 mg IM or 50% Dextrose (D50W) 50 mL IV. Seizures: Protect patient from injury, maintain airway, do NOT place anything in mouth! Status epilepticus (>5 min): Midazolam 5mg IM/buccal or Diazepam 5-10mg IV, call EMS.",
