    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nHigh-yield adverse interactions: 1) Non-selective beta-blockers (Propranolol) + Epinephrine -> unchecked alpha-1 vasoconstriction causing hypertensive spike and reflex bradycardia. 2) Metronidazole + Alcohol -> severe disulfiram reaction. 3) Metronidazole + Warfarin -> CYP2C9 inhibition causing extreme INR elevation and bleeding. 4) NSAIDs + ACE inhibitors/Diuretics -> renal failure and blunted antihypertensive effect. 5) Tetracyclines + Divalent cations (milk, antacids, iron) -> chelation and zero absorption.",
    "aiUnderstanding": "AI Conceptual Breakdown:\nThis page covers essential clinical and scientific concepts of Dental Pharmacology: Critical Drug-Drug Interactions in Dentistry. Understanding these foundational principles allows rapid recognition of Board examination question stems and clinical diagnostic dilemmas.",
