    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nPediatric medication rules: Clark's Rule: (Weight in lbs / 150) x Adult Dose. Young's Rule: (Age / [Age + 12]) x Adult Dose. Pediatric Local Anesthetic MRD: Children represent the highest risk demographic for fatal LA overdose due to low body weight; absolute carpule limits must be calculated prior to injection. Acetaminophen pediatric dose: 10-15 mg/kg every 4-6h. Ibuprofen pediatric dose: 5-10 mg/kg every 6-8h. Aspirin CONTRAINDICATED in viral illnesses due to Reye's Syndrome.",
