    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nGeriatric pharmacokinetic shifts: Decreased GFR and renal drug clearance, reduced hepatic blood flow and Phase I CYP450 oxidation, increased percentage of adipose tissue (prolongs half-life of lipid-soluble drugs like Diazepam), decreased serum albumin (increases free active fraction of Warfarin and NSAIDs). Clinical principle: 'Start low and go slow'. Severe anticholinergic burden from multiple medications induces severe xerostomia, caries, and confusion.",
