    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nComprehensive Board Exam Antidote Table: 1) Opioid toxicity -> Naloxone (Narcan). 2) Benzodiazepine toxicity -> Flumazenil (Romazicon). 3) Acetaminophen toxicity -> N-acetylcysteine (NAC). 4) Heparin toxicity -> Protamine sulfate. 5) Warfarin toxicity -> Vitamin K (Phytonadione). 6) Local Anesthetic Systemic Toxicity -> 20% Lipid Emulsion (Intralipid). 7) Methemoglobinemia -> Methylene Blue. 8) Organophosphate / Cholinergic crisis -> Atropine + Pralidoxime.",
