    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nAnesthetic delivery equipment & pharmacology: Topical Anesthesia (EMLA combination of Lidocaine + Prilocaine). Ester local anesthetics: Cocaine, Procaine (Novocaine), Benzocaine (Anbesol), Tetracaine, Propoxycaine. Most dental LAs are tertiary amines. Dental Needles: Ultra-short (<20mm, intraligamentary), Short (20mm), Long (32mm). Gauges: 30G (smallest), 27G, 25G (larger lumen, mandatory for high-risk positive aspiration like IAN blocks). Pain reduction occurs when anesthetic is warmed to body temperature (42\u00b0C). The 2mm bubble in the carpule is Nitrogen gas.",
