    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nDental nerve block anatomy: 1) PSA: blocks maxillary 2nd and 3rd molars and DB/palatal roots of 1st molar (NOT the MB root!). 2) MSA: blocks maxillary 1st molar MB root and 1st/2nd premolars. 3) ASA: blocks maxillary canines and incisors. 4) Infraorbital: blocks ASA + MSA and anterior facial soft tissues. 5) Nasopalatine: incisive foramen, blocks anterior 1/3 of hard palate canine to canine. 6) Greater Palatine: blocks posterior 2/3 of hard palate. 7) Classic Mandibular Block (IAN + Lingual): anesthetizes all mandibular teeth on injection side, buccal tissue anterior to 1st molar, anterior 2/3 of tongue, and floor of mouth.",
