    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nAdvanced mandibular block techniques: 1) Gow-Gates Technique: true mandibular nerve block targeting the lateral neck of the condyle just below the insertion of the lateral pterygoid muscle. Syringe aligned from contralateral premolar; blocks IAN, Lingual, Auriculotemporal, Mylohyoid, and Buccal nerves (entire V3 distribution!). Highest success rate, lowest aspiration rate. 2) Vazirani-Akinosi Technique: closed-mouth mandibular block indicated for patients with severe trismus or limited mouth opening where coronoid notch cannot be visualized; needle placed parallel to maxillary occlusal plane at level of mucogingival junction of maxillary 3rd molar.",
