    "summary": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nDental numbering systems: 1) Universal Numbering System (ADA): Permanent teeth numbered 1 to 32 (starts upper right 3rd molar #1 to upper left #16, down to lower left #17 to lower right #32); Primary teeth designated A to T (upper right primary 2nd molar A to upper left J, lower left K to lower right T). 2) Palmer's Notation (Zsigmondy): 4 quadrants with brackets; permanent teeth 1 to 8 per quadrant; primary teeth A to E. 3) FDI Two-Digit System (WHO): First digit = quadrant (1 to 4 permanent, 5 to 8 primary); Second digit = tooth position from midline (1 to 8 permanent, 1 to 5 primary).\n\nAI Conceptual Breakdown:\nThis page covers essential clinical and scientific concepts of Oral Anatomy: Tooth Numbering Systems & Anatomical Landmarks. Understanding these foundational principles allows rapid recognition of Board examination question stems and clinical diagnostic dilemmas.\n\nPRC Board Examination Pearl:\nFocus on high-yield hallmarks, diagnostic criteria, and standard clinical dosages/classifications associated with Oral Anatomy: Tooth Numbering Systems & Anatomical Landmarks.\n\nDr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Key lecture pearls, high-yield highlighted terms, and memory aids noted during DMF comprehensive board coaching.",
