    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nPosterior teeth and primary morphology: Mandibular 1st Molar (largest mandibular tooth, widest MD dimension of all teeth, 5 cusps [MB, DB, Distal, ML, DL], hexagonal occlusal outline, 2 broad roots M & D). Mandibular 2nd Molar (4 cusps of equal height, rectangular outline, cruciform '+' groove). Primary Dentition general hallmarks: crowns wider MD than crown height, prominent cervical bulges (Tubercle of Zuckerkandl), enamel and dentin half as thick as permanent teeth, pulp chambers relatively larger with high pulp horns, roots longer, more slender, and widely flared to encompass premolar buds.",
