    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nOcclusal concepts & morphology: Primary Canines & Molars. Working cusps (Maxillary Lingual, Mandibular Buccal) contact marginal ridges and central fossae; Non-working cusps (Maxillary Buccal, Mandibular Lingual) contact grooves and embrasures. Andrews 6 Keys to Normal Occlusion: 1) Class I molar relationship, 2) Crown angulation (mesiodistal tip), 3) Crown inclination (buccolingual torque), 4) No tooth rotation, 5) Tight proximal contacts, 6) Flat or mild Curve of Spee. Basic Jaw Relations: 1) Postural Position (muscle-guided, vertical dimension at rest, no tooth contact), 2) Centric Relation (CR: most superoanterior position of condyles in glenoid fossa, ligament-guided position).",
