    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nMandibular kinematics & occlusal curves: Centric Occlusion (CO / MI: complete tooth contact, tooth-guided position). Mandibular movements: Protrusive (forward movement, posterior teeth disarticulate: Christensen's phenomenon) and Lateral movement (working vs non-working sides). Guidance: Canine-guided (vertical overlap discludes all posterior teeth) vs Group function (multiple teeth contact on working side). Compensating Curvatures: Bonwill Equilateral Triangle (4 inches between condyles and incisal contact), Curve of Spee (anteroposterior curvature), Curve of Wilson (mediolateral curvature), Curve of Monson (3D sphere combining Spee and Wilson). Functions of stomatognathic system: Mastication, Deglutition, Respiration, Speech, Proprioception.",
