    "summary": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nMandibular kinematics & occlusal curves: Centric Occlusion (CO / MI: complete tooth contact, tooth-guided position). Mandibular movements: Protrusive (forward movement, posterior teeth disarticulate: Christensen's phenomenon) and Lateral movement (working vs non-working sides). Guidance: Canine-guided (vertical overlap discludes all posterior teeth) vs Group function (multiple teeth contact on working side). Compensating Curvatures: Bonwill Equilateral Triangle (4 inches between condyles and incisal contact), Curve of Spee (anteroposterior curvature), Curve of Wilson (mediolateral curvature), Curve of Monson (3D sphere combining Spee and Wilson). Functions of stomatognathic system: Mastication, Deglutition, Respiration, Speech, Proprioception.\n\nAI Conceptual Breakdown:\nThis page covers essential clinical and scientific concepts of Centric Occlusion, Mandibular Movements & Compensating Curvatures. Understanding these foundational principles allows rapid recognition of Board examination question stems and clinical diagnostic dilemmas.\n\nPRC Board Examination Pearl:\nFocus on high-yield hallmarks, diagnostic criteria, and standard clinical dosages/classifications associated with Centric Occlusion, Mandibular Movements & Compensating Curvatures.\n\nDr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Key lecture pearls, high-yield highlighted terms, and memory aids noted during DMF comprehensive board coaching.",
