    "summary": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nDMF Orthodontics Chapter Start by Dr. Mickhail Q. Francisco: Classification of Malocclusion according to Edward Angle: 1) Class I (Neutroclusion): MB cusp of maxillary 1st molar occludes in buccal groove of mandibular 1st molar; Dewey types 1-5 (anterior crowding, labioversion, anterior crossbite, posterior crossbite, mesial drift). 2) Class II (Distocclusion / Retrognathism): MB cusp of max 1st molar falls between mand 1st molar and 2nd premolar; Div 1 (extreme labioversion/overjet), Div 2 (palatally tipped centrals, labially tipped laterals, deep bite). 3) Class III (Mesiocclusion / Prognathism): MB cusp falls between mand 1st and 2nd molars. Signs of Incipient Malocclusion: lack of interdental spacing in primary dentition, crowding of permanent incisors in mixed dentition, premature loss of primary canines.\n\nAI Conceptual Breakdown:\nThis page covers essential clinical and scientific concepts of Orthodontics: Angle's Classification of Malocclusion & Incipient Signs. Understanding these foundational principles allows rapid recognition of Board examination question stems and clinical diagnostic dilemmas.\n\nPRC Board Examination Pearl:\nFocus on high-yield hallmarks, diagnostic criteria, and standard clinical dosages/classifications associated with Orthodontics: Angle's Classification of Malocclusion & Incipient Signs.\n\nDr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Key lecture pearls, high-yield highlighted terms, and memory aids noted during DMF comprehensive board coaching.",
