    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nOrthodontic diagnostics & cephalometrics: Malocclusion and Speech difficulties (S, Z sibilants associated with anterior open bite / excessive overjet; T, D with irregular incisors; F, V with skeletal Class III; B, P, M with cleft lip). Cephalometrics intro ('Poor-man's cephalometrics' = facial profile analysis). Key Cephalometric Landmarks: S (Sella, most stable landmark in cranial base), N (Nasion), Bo (Bolton), Ba (Basion), Ar (Articulare), Po (Porion), Or (Orbitale), Point A (Subspinale: premaxilla base), Point B (Supramentale: mandible base), Pog (Pogonion: most anterior chin), Me (Menton: most inferior symphysis), Go (Gonion). Planes: Frankfort Horizontal Plane (Porion to Orbitale), Sella-Nasion Plane, Mandibular Plane (Menton to Gonion).",
