    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nCephalometric angles & orthopedic headgears: FMA (Frankfort Mandibular Plane Angle, normal 28.7\u00b0 \u00b1 5.8\u00b0; steep = open bite / Class II; flat = deep bite / Class III). ANB angle (normal 2.5\u00b0 \u00b1 2.5\u00b0; >5\u00b0 = Skeletal Class II; <0\u00b0 = Skeletal Class III). SNA & SNB. Tweed's Triangle (FMA, IMPA, FMIA). Removable appliances: produce tipping movements; components: Adams clasp, ball clasp, baseplate, finger springs. Extraoral Headgears for Skeletal Class II: High-pull (distal & intrusive on molars/maxilla), Cervical-pull (distal & extrusive), Straight-pull. Reverse-pull Headgear (Facemask) for Skeletal Class III to protract maxilla; Chin Cup to redirect mandibular growth.",
