    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nGrowth modification & fixed mechanics: Functional Appliances: Tooth-borne (Activator advances mandible edge-to-edge; Bionator trimmed down; Herbst telescopic pin-and-tube; Twin Block) vs Tissue-borne (Frankel Functional Regulator: ONLY tissue-borne appliance, alters facial soft tissue posture). Wire Bending Orders: 1st order (in/out, facial/lingual, rotational), 2nd order (tip, mesial/distal), 3rd order (torque, root inclination). Fixed Appliances history: Pin and tube (1910), Ribbon arch (1915), Begg, Edgewise (1925), PEA / Straight-wire brackets. Banding with Glass Ionomer; Bonding with 35-50% Phosphoric acid etch (Buonocore 1955) and Bis-GMA resin (Bowen 1962).",
