    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nBiomaterials & crossbite mechanics: Archwire properties (high strength, low stiffness, high range, high formability): Stainless Steel (18% Cr, 8% Ni; high stiffness), Cobalt-Chromium (Elgiloy), Ni-Ti (Nitinol shape memory and superelasticity), Beta-Titanium (TMA: excellent formability and moderate force). Intermaxillary Elastics: Class I (space closure), Class II (treats Class II), Class III (treats Class III). Crossbites: Buccal, Lingual, Posterior (abnormal buccolingual relation). Treatment by Palatal Expansion: Pre-adolescents (<12y: W-arch, Quad-Helix, split plates with jackscrew); Adolescents (>12y: Rapid Palatal Expanders / Hyrax). Anterior Crossbite: Dental (1-2 teeth: tongue blade, inclined plane, Hawley with springs), Skeletal (>3 teeth: Class III protraction), Functional (pseudoclass III).",
