    "originalPrint": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nDeleterious habits & habit appliances: Thumbsucking habit triad: Duration, Frequency, Intensity. Age <=4 years: observe, no treatment; Age 4-6 years: habit must cease before permanent incisors erupt. Consequence: anterior open bite, constricted maxilla, Class II malocclusion. Appliances: Bluegrass appliance, Palatal crib, thumb guard. Tongue Thrusting: tongue protrudes during swallowing/speech/rest (infantile swallowing persists beyond 18 mo); treated with Tongue crib. Space Maintainers: passive appliances preventing mesial drifting of permanent 1st molars. Best space maintainer is a well-restored natural tooth! Band and Loop: unilateral single tooth loss.",
