    "summary": "Original Printed Textbook Content:\nSpace management & mixed dentition milestones: Space maintainers: Lingual Holding Arch (bilateral mandibular tooth loss, requires erupted permanent incisors), Distal Shoe (early loss of primary 2nd molar BEFORE permanent 1st molar erupts; intra-alveolar guide blade), Transpalatal Arch (TPA), Nance appliance. Primary Molar Relationships: Flush terminal plane (normal cusp-to-cusp permanent 6; shifts into Class I by mesial shift), Distal step (leads to Class II), Mesial step (leads to Class I). Nance Leeway Space: MD width difference between primary C-D-E and permanent 3-4-5 (Mandible = 1.7\u20132.5mm per quad; Maxilla = 0.9\u20131.5mm per quad). Primate Spaces: Maxillary = MESIAL to canine; Mandibular = DISTAL to canine.\n\nAI Conceptual Breakdown:\nThis page covers essential clinical and scientific concepts of Pediatric Orthodontics: Space Maintainers, Primary Terminal Planes & Leeway Space. Understanding these foundational principles allows rapid recognition of Board examination question stems and clinical diagnostic dilemmas.\n\nPRC Board Examination Pearl:\nFocus on high-yield hallmarks, diagnostic criteria, and standard clinical dosages/classifications associated with Pediatric Orthodontics: Space Maintainers, Primary Terminal Planes & Leeway Space.\n\nDr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Key lecture pearls, high-yield highlighted terms, and memory aids noted during DMF comprehensive board coaching.",
