    "originalPrint": "Oral Fungal & Treponemal Infections:\n- Oral Candidiasis (Candida albicans):\n  * Pseudomembranous ('Thrush'): White curd-like plaques on buccal mucosa/tongue that WIPE OFF with gauze, leaving an underlying erythematous bleeding surface.\n  * Erythematous (Atrophic): Red mucosal patch; Common under acrylic dentures ('Denture Stomatitis' / chronic atrophic candidiasis) or after broad-spectrum antibiotics ('Antibiotic sore mouth').\n  * Chronic Hyperplastic (Candidal Leukoplakia): White plaque that DOES NOT wipe off; High malignant potential.\n  * Angular Cheilitis: Erythema and fissuring at lip commissures; Candida + Staph aureus.\n  * Treatment: Nystatin oral suspension, Clotrimazole troches, Fluconazole.\n- Syphilis (Treponema pallidum):\n  * Primary Syphilis: CHANCRE (solitary, painless, indurated ulcer at inoculation site, e.g. lip; resolves in 3-8 weeks).\n  * Secondary Syphilis: MUCOUS PATCHES (highly infectious snail-track ulcers) and Condyloma Lata.\n  * Tertiary Syphilis: GUMMA (destructive granulomatous lesion perforating the hard palate); Syphilitic glossitis.\n  * Congenital Syphilis: Hutchinson's Triad (Hutchinson's incisors / screwdriver-shaped incisors, Mulberry molars, Eighth nerve deafness, Interstitial keratitis).",
    "aiUnderstanding": "AI Conceptual Breakdown:\nCandida albicans exists as a harmless commensal blastospore in 50% of healthy mouths. Impairment of salivary flow, topical steroids, broad-spectrum antibiotics (suppressing competing oral flora), or immunosuppression triggers dimorphic transition into invasive, hyphae-forming pseudomycelia that invade the superficial keratin layer. Syphilis's tertiary gumma causes severe endarteritis obliterans: ischemia of the midpalatal suture leads to full-thickness palatal perforation into the nasal cavity.",
    "boardPearls": "PRC Board Pearl:\nPseudomembranous candidiasis WIPES OFF leaving a raw bleeding base! Congenital syphilis: Hutchinson's Triad (Hutchinson's notched incisors + Mulberry molars + 8th nerve deafness + Interstitial keratitis). Primary syphilis lesion is the painless CHANCRE.",
    "leaneNotes": "Dr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Thrush / Pseudomembranous Candidiasis = WIPES OFF leaving bleeding surface!\n* Primary Syphilis = CHANCRE (painless indurated ulcer).\n* Congenital Syphilis = Hutchinson's screwdriver incisors + Mulberry molars + Deafness!",
    "summary": "Oral Fungal & Treponemal Infections:\n- Oral Candidiasis (Candida albicans):\n  * Pseudomembranous ('Thrush'): White curd-like plaques on buccal mucosa/tongue that WIPE OFF with gauze, leaving an underlying erythematous bleeding surface.\n  * Erythematous (Atrophic): Red mucosal patch; Common under acrylic dentures ('Denture Stomatitis' / chronic atrophic candidiasis) or after broad-spectrum antibiotics ('Antibiotic sore mouth').\n  * Chronic Hyperplastic (Candidal Leukoplakia): White plaque that DOES NOT wipe off; High malignant potential.\n  * Angular Cheilitis: Erythema and fissuring at lip commissures; Candida + Staph aureus.\n  * Treatment: Nystatin oral suspension, Clotrimazole troches, Fluconazole.\n- Syphilis (Treponema pallidum):\n  * Primary Syphilis: CHANCRE (solitary, painless, indurated ulcer at inoculation site, e.g. lip; resolves in 3-8 weeks).\n  * Secondary Syphilis: MUCOUS PATCHES (highly infectious snail-track ulcers) and Condyloma Lata.\n  * Tertiary Syphilis: GUMMA (destructive granulomatous lesion perforating the hard palate); Syphilitic glossitis.\n  * Congenital Syphilis: Hutchinson's Triad (Hutchinson's incisors / screwdriver-shaped incisors, Mulberry molars, Eighth nerve deafness, Interstitial keratitis).\n\nAI Conceptual Breakdown:\nCandida albicans exists as a harmless commensal blastospore in 50% of healthy mouths. Impairment of salivary flow, topical steroids, broad-spectrum antibiotics (suppressing competing oral flora), or immunosuppression triggers dimorphic transition into invasive, hyphae-forming pseudomycelia that invade the superficial keratin layer. Syphilis's tertiary gumma causes severe endarteritis obliterans: ischemia of the midpalatal suture leads to full-thickness palatal perforation into the nasal cavity.\n\nPRC Board Pearl:\nPseudomembranous candidiasis WIPES OFF leaving a raw bleeding base! Congenital syphilis: Hutchinson's Triad (Hutchinson's notched incisors + Mulberry molars + 8th nerve deafness + Interstitial keratitis). Primary syphilis lesion is the painless CHANCRE.\n\nDr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Thrush / Pseudomembranous Candidiasis = WIPES OFF leaving bleeding surface!\n* Primary Syphilis = CHANCRE (painless indurated ulcer).\n* Congenital Syphilis = Hutchinson's screwdriver incisors + Mulberry molars + Deafness!",
