    "originalPrint": "SCC Histopathology & AJCC TNM Staging:\n- Histopathologic Characteristics:\n  * Invasive islands, cords, and sheets of malignant squamous epithelial cells breaching the basement membrane into the underlying connective tissue stroma.\n  * Cellular & Nuclear Atypia: Pleomorphism, hyperchromatism, increased nuclear-to-cytoplasmic (N:C) ratio, atypical mitotic figures.\n  * KERATIN PEARLS (epithelial pearls / horn pearls): Concentric whorls of laminated eosinophilic keratin produced within malignant epithelial islands (hallmark of well-differentiated SCC).\n- AJCC TNM Staging System:\n  * T (Tumor Size / Depth):\n    - T1: Tumor <= 2 cm (and DOI <= 5mm).\n    - T2: Tumor > 2 cm but <= 4 cm.\n    - T3: Tumor > 4 cm.\n    - T4: Advanced tumor invading adjacent deep structures (cortical bone, deep tongue muscle, maxillary sinus, skin).\n  * N (Regional Lymph Nodes): N0 (no regional metastasis), N1 (single ipsilateral <=3cm), N2, N3.\n  * M (Distant Metastasis): M0 (no distant metastasis), M1 (distant metastasis present - lungs, liver, bone).",
    "aiUnderstanding": "AI Conceptual Breakdown:\nTNM stage is the single most reliable prognostic indicator of patient survival. Oral SCC metastasizes primarily through lymphatic vessels to the deep cervical lymph node chain. Once malignant cells breach cervical lymph node capsules (extranodal extension), 5-year survival drops by 50%. Histologic grade (keratin pearls, differentiation) reflects cellular maturity, but TNM stage dictates whether wide local resection, neck dissection, and adjuvant chemoradiotherapy are required.",
    "boardPearls": "PRC Board Pearl:\nHistologic hallmark of well-differentiated Squamous Cell Carcinoma: KERATIN PEARLS (concentric whorls of keratin)! TNM definitions: T1 is <= 2cm; T2 is 2-4cm; T3 is > 4cm. Most common site of distant metastasis: LUNGS.",
    "leaneNotes": "Dr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* KERATIN PEARLS = well-differentiated SCC histology!\n* T1 <= 2cm; T2 = 2-4cm; T3 > 4cm; T4 = invading bone/muscle!\n* Cancer spreads first to cervical neck lymph nodes.",
    "summary": "SCC Histopathology & AJCC TNM Staging:\n- Histopathologic Characteristics:\n  * Invasive islands, cords, and sheets of malignant squamous epithelial cells breaching the basement membrane into the underlying connective tissue stroma.\n  * Cellular & Nuclear Atypia: Pleomorphism, hyperchromatism, increased nuclear-to-cytoplasmic (N:C) ratio, atypical mitotic figures.\n  * KERATIN PEARLS (epithelial pearls / horn pearls): Concentric whorls of laminated eosinophilic keratin produced within malignant epithelial islands (hallmark of well-differentiated SCC).\n- AJCC TNM Staging System:\n  * T (Tumor Size / Depth):\n    - T1: Tumor <= 2 cm (and DOI <= 5mm).\n    - T2: Tumor > 2 cm but <= 4 cm.\n    - T3: Tumor > 4 cm.\n    - T4: Advanced tumor invading adjacent deep structures (cortical bone, deep tongue muscle, maxillary sinus, skin).\n  * N (Regional Lymph Nodes): N0 (no regional metastasis), N1 (single ipsilateral <=3cm), N2, N3.\n  * M (Distant Metastasis): M0 (no distant metastasis), M1 (distant metastasis present - lungs, liver, bone).\n\nAI Conceptual Breakdown:\nTNM stage is the single most reliable prognostic indicator of patient survival. Oral SCC metastasizes primarily through lymphatic vessels to the deep cervical lymph node chain. Once malignant cells breach cervical lymph node capsules (extranodal extension), 5-year survival drops by 50%. Histologic grade (keratin pearls, differentiation) reflects cellular maturity, but TNM stage dictates whether wide local resection, neck dissection, and adjuvant chemoradiotherapy are required.\n\nPRC Board Pearl:\nHistologic hallmark of well-differentiated Squamous Cell Carcinoma: KERATIN PEARLS (concentric whorls of keratin)! TNM definitions: T1 is <= 2cm; T2 is 2-4cm; T3 is > 4cm. Most common site of distant metastasis: LUNGS.\n\nDr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* KERATIN PEARLS = well-differentiated SCC histology!\n* T1 <= 2cm; T2 = 2-4cm; T3 > 4cm; T4 = invading bone/muscle!\n* Cancer spreads first to cervical neck lymph nodes.",
