    "originalPrint": "Endodontic Access Cavity Preparation & Canal Morphology:\n- Primary Objective: Obtain STRAIGHT-LINE ACCESS to the apical third of root canals; De-roof pulp chamber completely, expose all canal orifices, conserve tooth structure.\n- Access Outlines by Tooth Group:\n  * Maxillary Central Incisor: Rounded TRIANGULAR access (base towards incisal edge, apex towards cingulum); Completely removes pulp horns.\n  * Maxillary Premolars: Oval / Elliptical access oriented BUCCOLINGUALLY.\n  * Maxillary First Molar:\n    - Access Shape: RHOMBOID or Rounded Triangle (located in mesial 2/3 of crown; do NOT cross oblique ridge unless involved by caries).\n    - Canals (3 or 4): Mesiobuccal-1 (MB1), Distobuccal (DB), Palatal (P), and MESIOBUCCAL-2 (MB2).\n    - MB2 Canal: Present in >70% to 90% of maxillary first molars; Located palatal and slightly mesial to the MB1 orifice along a groove connecting MB1 to Palatal.\n  * Mandibular First Molar:\n    - Access Shape: TRAPEZOIDAL or Rectangular (wider on mesial, tapered on distal).\n    - Canals (3 or 4): Mesiobuccal (MB), Mesiolingual (ML), Distal (or Distobuccal + Distolingual).",
    "aiUnderstanding": "AI Conceptual Breakdown:\nStraight-line access prevents file deflection. If the cervical dentin shelf (coronal overhang) is not flared, instruments bend abruptly upon entering the orifice, predisposing the file to cyclic fatigue and instrument separation, apical canal transportation, or ledging. The high failure rate of maxillary molar endodontics historically was driven by missing the MB2 canal, which harbors necrotic tissue in >70% of clinical cases.",
    "boardPearls": "PRC Board Pearl:\nAccess shape for Maxillary Central Incisor: Rounded TRIANGULAR! Access shape for Maxillary First Molar: Rounded triangular / Rhomboid (MB2 canal present in >70-90%). Access shape for Mandibular First Molar: Trapezoidal.",
    "leaneNotes": "Dr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Upper central incisor access = TRIANGLE (base towards biting edge).\n* Upper 1st molar access = RHOMBOID / Rounded triangle (LOOK FOR MB2 CANAL! >70% have it!).\n* Lower 1st molar access = TRAPEZOID.",
    "summary": "Endodontic Access Cavity Preparation & Canal Morphology:\n- Primary Objective: Obtain STRAIGHT-LINE ACCESS to the apical third of root canals; De-roof pulp chamber completely, expose all canal orifices, conserve tooth structure.\n- Access Outlines by Tooth Group:\n  * Maxillary Central Incisor: Rounded TRIANGULAR access (base towards incisal edge, apex towards cingulum); Completely removes pulp horns.\n  * Maxillary Premolars: Oval / Elliptical access oriented BUCCOLINGUALLY.\n  * Maxillary First Molar:\n    - Access Shape: RHOMBOID or Rounded Triangle (located in mesial 2/3 of crown; do NOT cross oblique ridge unless involved by caries).\n    - Canals (3 or 4): Mesiobuccal-1 (MB1), Distobuccal (DB), Palatal (P), and MESIOBUCCAL-2 (MB2).\n    - MB2 Canal: Present in >70% to 90% of maxillary first molars; Located palatal and slightly mesial to the MB1 orifice along a groove connecting MB1 to Palatal.\n  * Mandibular First Molar:\n    - Access Shape: TRAPEZOIDAL or Rectangular (wider on mesial, tapered on distal).\n    - Canals (3 or 4): Mesiobuccal (MB), Mesiolingual (ML), Distal (or Distobuccal + Distolingual).\n\nAI Conceptual Breakdown:\nStraight-line access prevents file deflection. If the cervical dentin shelf (coronal overhang) is not flared, instruments bend abruptly upon entering the orifice, predisposing the file to cyclic fatigue and instrument separation, apical canal transportation, or ledging. The high failure rate of maxillary molar endodontics historically was driven by missing the MB2 canal, which harbors necrotic tissue in >70% of clinical cases.\n\nPRC Board Pearl:\nAccess shape for Maxillary Central Incisor: Rounded TRIANGULAR! Access shape for Maxillary First Molar: Rounded triangular / Rhomboid (MB2 canal present in >70-90%). Access shape for Mandibular First Molar: Trapezoidal.\n\nDr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Upper central incisor access = TRIANGLE (base towards biting edge).\n* Upper 1st molar access = RHOMBOID / Rounded triangle (LOOK FOR MB2 CANAL! >70% have it!).\n* Lower 1st molar access = TRAPEZOID.",
