    "originalPrint": "Intracanal Medicaments & Coronal Sealing:\n- Calcium Hydroxide [Ca(OH)2]:\n  * Gold standard interappointment intracanal medicament for multi-visit root canal therapy.\n  * Mechanism: Ultra-high alkaline pH (~12.5); Releases hydroxyl ions (OH-) that:\n    1. Damages bacterial cell membranes by lipid peroxidation.\n    2. Denatures bacterial enzymes and structural proteins.\n    3. Inactivates bacterial Lipopolysaccharide (LPS / endotoxin) in necrotic canals.\n    4. Stimulates alkaline phosphatase, inducing hard tissue calcific barrier formation.\n  * Placement: Minimum 7 to 14 days in canal for maximal bactericidal efficacy.\n- Triple Antibiotic Paste (TAP - used in Regenerative Endodontics):\n  * Ciprofloxacin + Metronidazole + Minocycline (causes tooth discoloration; can substitute Cefaclor).\n- Temporary Restorations (Coronal Seal):\n  * Cavit: Zinc oxide/calcium sulfate base; Sets by hygroscopic expansion upon water absorption; Minimum 3.5 to 4.0 mm thickness required to prevent coronal microleakage.\n  * IRM (Intermediate Restorative Material): Polymer-reinforced ZOE.",
    "aiUnderstanding": "AI Conceptual Breakdown:\nGram-negative anaerobic bacteria shed lipopolysaccharide (endotoxin) into dentinal tubules, perpetuating periapical bone resorption via TLR-4 macrophage activation. Conventional antibiotics and irrigants fail to destroy lipid-A endotoxin cores. Calcium hydroxide's extreme alkalinity (pH 12.5) hydrolyzes ester bonds within lipid A, chemically detoxifying LPS and extinguishing periapical bone destruction.",
    "boardPearls": "PRC Board Pearl:\nMechanism of Calcium Hydroxide: Ultra-high alkaline pH (~12.5) that denatures bacterial proteins and detoxifies LPS endotoxin! Minimum thickness for Cavit temporary restoration to prevent bacterial leakage: 3.5 to 4.0 mm.",
    "leaneNotes": "Dr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Calcium Hydroxide pH = 12.5! (Kills bacteria & neutralizes LPS endotoxins).\n* Leave in canal for at least 7 to 14 days between visits.\n* Cavit temporary filling MUST be at least 3.5 to 4.0 mm THICK!",
    "summary": "Intracanal Medicaments & Coronal Sealing:\n- Calcium Hydroxide [Ca(OH)2]:\n  * Gold standard interappointment intracanal medicament for multi-visit root canal therapy.\n  * Mechanism: Ultra-high alkaline pH (~12.5); Releases hydroxyl ions (OH-) that:\n    1. Damages bacterial cell membranes by lipid peroxidation.\n    2. Denatures bacterial enzymes and structural proteins.\n    3. Inactivates bacterial Lipopolysaccharide (LPS / endotoxin) in necrotic canals.\n    4. Stimulates alkaline phosphatase, inducing hard tissue calcific barrier formation.\n  * Placement: Minimum 7 to 14 days in canal for maximal bactericidal efficacy.\n- Triple Antibiotic Paste (TAP - used in Regenerative Endodontics):\n  * Ciprofloxacin + Metronidazole + Minocycline (causes tooth discoloration; can substitute Cefaclor).\n- Temporary Restorations (Coronal Seal):\n  * Cavit: Zinc oxide/calcium sulfate base; Sets by hygroscopic expansion upon water absorption; Minimum 3.5 to 4.0 mm thickness required to prevent coronal microleakage.\n  * IRM (Intermediate Restorative Material): Polymer-reinforced ZOE.\n\nAI Conceptual Breakdown:\nGram-negative anaerobic bacteria shed lipopolysaccharide (endotoxin) into dentinal tubules, perpetuating periapical bone resorption via TLR-4 macrophage activation. Conventional antibiotics and irrigants fail to destroy lipid-A endotoxin cores. Calcium hydroxide's extreme alkalinity (pH 12.5) hydrolyzes ester bonds within lipid A, chemically detoxifying LPS and extinguishing periapical bone destruction.\n\nPRC Board Pearl:\nMechanism of Calcium Hydroxide: Ultra-high alkaline pH (~12.5) that denatures bacterial proteins and detoxifies LPS endotoxin! Minimum thickness for Cavit temporary restoration to prevent bacterial leakage: 3.5 to 4.0 mm.\n\nDr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Calcium Hydroxide pH = 12.5! (Kills bacteria & neutralizes LPS endotoxins).\n* Leave in canal for at least 7 to 14 days between visits.\n* Cavit temporary filling MUST be at least 3.5 to 4.0 mm THICK!",
