    "originalPrint": "Non-Surgical Periodontal Therapy: SRP & Ultrasonics:\n- Definitions:\n  * Scaling: Instrumentation of crown and root surfaces to remove plaque, calculus, and stains.\n  * Root Planing: Definitive treatment procedure designed to remove rough, altered cementum contaminated with toxins and create a smooth, clean root surface to facilitate biological reattachment.\n- Ultrasonic Scaler Technologies:\n  1. Magnetostrictive (e.g., Cavitron):\n     * Stack of ferromagnetic nickel alloy strips or ferrite rod expands and contracts in magnetic field.\n     * Frequency: 20,000 to 42,000 Hz (cycles/sec); Tip motion: ELLIPTICAL (all surfaces of tip are active: back, face, lateral sides).\n  2. Piezoelectric:\n     * Ceramic crystal transducers expand/contract in alternating electric field.\n     * Frequency: 25,000 to 50,000 Hz; Tip motion: LINEAR (back-and-forth; only the two lateral edges of tip are active).\n- Biophysical Cleaning Mechanisms of Ultrasonics:\n  * Mechanical Vibration: Physical fracturing of calculus.\n  * Cavitation: Rapid formation and collapse of microscopic vapor bubbles in cooling water spray, releasing shockwaves that rupture bacterial cell walls.\n  * Acoustic Microstreaming: Vigorous swirling fluid currents that flush out subgingival biofilms.",
    "aiUnderstanding": "AI Conceptual Breakdown:\nUltrasonic scalers eliminate subgingival biofilms through acoustic energy. Cavitation occurs when high-frequency tip oscillations generate localized negative pressure zones in water, creating micro-bubbles that implode instantaneously. These implosions generate shockwaves exceeding 1,000 atmospheres of pressure, mechanically lysing bacterial cell membranes in inaccessible furcations without requiring direct instrument contact.",
    "boardPearls": "PRC Board Pearl:\nMagnetostrictive tip moves in an: ELLIPTICAL motion (all sides active). Piezoelectric tip moves in a: LINEAR back-and-forth motion (only lateral sides active). Cavitation is the collapse of microscopic bubbles in water releasing shockwaves that destroy bacteria.",
    "leaneNotes": "Dr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Magnetostrictive (Cavitron) = ELLIPTICAL motion (all tip sides active).\n* Piezoelectric = LINEAR motion (lateral sides only).\n* Cavitation = water bubbles pop and blast bacteria apart!",
    "summary": "Non-Surgical Periodontal Therapy: SRP & Ultrasonics:\n- Definitions:\n  * Scaling: Instrumentation of crown and root surfaces to remove plaque, calculus, and stains.\n  * Root Planing: Definitive treatment procedure designed to remove rough, altered cementum contaminated with toxins and create a smooth, clean root surface to facilitate biological reattachment.\n- Ultrasonic Scaler Technologies:\n  1. Magnetostrictive (e.g., Cavitron):\n     * Stack of ferromagnetic nickel alloy strips or ferrite rod expands and contracts in magnetic field.\n     * Frequency: 20,000 to 42,000 Hz (cycles/sec); Tip motion: ELLIPTICAL (all surfaces of tip are active: back, face, lateral sides).\n  2. Piezoelectric:\n     * Ceramic crystal transducers expand/contract in alternating electric field.\n     * Frequency: 25,000 to 50,000 Hz; Tip motion: LINEAR (back-and-forth; only the two lateral edges of tip are active).\n- Biophysical Cleaning Mechanisms of Ultrasonics:\n  * Mechanical Vibration: Physical fracturing of calculus.\n  * Cavitation: Rapid formation and collapse of microscopic vapor bubbles in cooling water spray, releasing shockwaves that rupture bacterial cell walls.\n  * Acoustic Microstreaming: Vigorous swirling fluid currents that flush out subgingival biofilms.\n\nAI Conceptual Breakdown:\nUltrasonic scalers eliminate subgingival biofilms through acoustic energy. Cavitation occurs when high-frequency tip oscillations generate localized negative pressure zones in water, creating micro-bubbles that implode instantaneously. These implosions generate shockwaves exceeding 1,000 atmospheres of pressure, mechanically lysing bacterial cell membranes in inaccessible furcations without requiring direct instrument contact.\n\nPRC Board Pearl:\nMagnetostrictive tip moves in an: ELLIPTICAL motion (all sides active). Piezoelectric tip moves in a: LINEAR back-and-forth motion (only lateral sides active). Cavitation is the collapse of microscopic bubbles in water releasing shockwaves that destroy bacteria.\n\nDr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Magnetostrictive (Cavitron) = ELLIPTICAL motion (all tip sides active).\n* Piezoelectric = LINEAR motion (lateral sides only).\n* Cavitation = water bubbles pop and blast bacteria apart!",
