    "originalPrint": "Dental Licensure Examination & Qualifications of Examinees:\n- Qualifications of Applicant for Examination (Section 14, RA 9484):\n  1. Citizen of the Philippines, or foreign citizen whose country grants reciprocity to Filipino dentists.\n  2. Good moral character.\n  3. Graduate of a recognized dental school/college conferring Doctor of Dental Medicine (DDM) degree.\n  4. Completed mandatory internship / clinical requirements.\n- Two-Part Examination Structure:\n  * Part I: Written / Theoretical Examination (Day 1 Basic Sciences, Day 2 Clinical Dentistry & Pharmacology, Day 3 Specialized Disciplines).\n  * Part II: Practical / Clinical Performance Examination (Operative Dentistry, Prosthodontics, Endodontics, Complete Denture setup).\n- Refresher Course Rule (Section 16):\n  * Any candidate who FAILS THREE (3) CONSECUTIVE dental licensure examinations shall NOT be allowed to take the examination for the fourth time without submitting proof of completion of a recognized REFRESHER COURSE for at least ONE (1) YEAR in an accredited dental school.",
    "aiUnderstanding": "AI Conceptual Breakdown:\nThe refresher course mandate protects the public from chronic incompetence. After three consecutive examination failures, the law presumes significant gaps in foundational knowledge or clinical motor skills. Mandating a 1-year academic and clinical refresher ensures remediation before re-challenging the licensure gate.",
    "boardPearls": "PRC Board Pearl:\nHow many consecutive failures trigger the Refresher Course requirement? THREE (3) consecutive failures! The refresher course must be completed for at least ONE (1) YEAR in an accredited dental institution before taking the exam a 4th time.",
    "leaneNotes": "Dr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Fail 3 TIMES consecutively -> MUST take 1-YEAR REFRESHER COURSE!\n* Exam has two parts: Written (Theory) and Practical (Hands-on clinical).\n* You are going to PASS on your first take, Dr. Leane! \ud83e\ude7a\ud83d\udc9c",
    "summary": "Dental Licensure Examination & Qualifications of Examinees:\n- Qualifications of Applicant for Examination (Section 14, RA 9484):\n  1. Citizen of the Philippines, or foreign citizen whose country grants reciprocity to Filipino dentists.\n  2. Good moral character.\n  3. Graduate of a recognized dental school/college conferring Doctor of Dental Medicine (DDM) degree.\n  4. Completed mandatory internship / clinical requirements.\n- Two-Part Examination Structure:\n  * Part I: Written / Theoretical Examination (Day 1 Basic Sciences, Day 2 Clinical Dentistry & Pharmacology, Day 3 Specialized Disciplines).\n  * Part II: Practical / Clinical Performance Examination (Operative Dentistry, Prosthodontics, Endodontics, Complete Denture setup).\n- Refresher Course Rule (Section 16):\n  * Any candidate who FAILS THREE (3) CONSECUTIVE dental licensure examinations shall NOT be allowed to take the examination for the fourth time without submitting proof of completion of a recognized REFRESHER COURSE for at least ONE (1) YEAR in an accredited dental school.\n\nAI Conceptual Breakdown:\nThe refresher course mandate protects the public from chronic incompetence. After three consecutive examination failures, the law presumes significant gaps in foundational knowledge or clinical motor skills. Mandating a 1-year academic and clinical refresher ensures remediation before re-challenging the licensure gate.\n\nPRC Board Pearl:\nHow many consecutive failures trigger the Refresher Course requirement? THREE (3) consecutive failures! The refresher course must be completed for at least ONE (1) YEAR in an accredited dental institution before taking the exam a 4th time.\n\nDr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Fail 3 TIMES consecutively -> MUST take 1-YEAR REFRESHER COURSE!\n* Exam has two parts: Written (Theory) and Practical (Hands-on clinical).\n* You are going to PASS on your first take, Dr. Leane! \ud83e\ude7a\ud83d\udc9c",
