    "pageNumber": 259,
    "title": "The Dentist as an Expert Witness & Medicolegal Evidence",
    "subject": "Dental Jurisprudence",
    "day": "Day 3 (11:00 AM \u2022 10%) - Jurisprudence & Ethics",
    "author": "Atty. Marvin Joseph M. Ocampo",
    "keywords": [
      "expert witness",
      "ordinary witness",
      "medicolegal evidence",
      "opinion rule",
      "subpoena",
      "daubert standard"
    ],
    "originalPrint": "The Dentist as an Expert Witness & Medical Testimony:\n- Ordinary Witness vs Expert Witness:\n  * Ordinary (Fact) Witness: Can testify ONLY to facts personally perceived by their own senses (what they saw, heard, felt); CANNOT give opinions or conclusions.\n  * Expert Witness: A person possessing SPECIAL KNOWLEDGE, skill, experience, training, or education in a particular science, art, or profession;\n    - Exception to the Opinion Rule: An expert witness IS PERMITTED TO GIVE OPINIONS, deductions, and conclusions based on hypothetical questions or scientific evidence presented in court!\n- Role of Dental Expert Witness:\n  * To assist the judge and court in understanding complex medical, dental, and biomechanical evidence.\n  * Must be objective and impartial; Not an advocate for either party.\n  * Evaluates whether the defendant dentist adhered to or breached the recognized 'standard of care' in the specific specialty.",
    "aiUnderstanding": "AI Conceptual Breakdown:\nUnder the Rules of Court, opinion evidence is inadmissible because drawing conclusions is the exclusive prerogative of the judge. The Expert Witness is the sole legal exception: because dental diagnosis and surgical technique lie beyond the knowledge of ordinary laypersons, an expert dentist is empowered to interpret radiographs, evaluate surgical technique, and state whether an outcome stemmed from negligence or known biological risk.",
    "boardPearls": "PRC Board Pearl:\nDifference between Ordinary and Expert Witness: An Expert Witness is legally permitted to give OPINIONS and conclusions within their field of expertise! Ordinary witnesses can testify only to facts personally perceived.",
    "leaneNotes": "Dr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Ordinary witness = tells what they saw/heard only (NO OPINIONS!).\n* Expert witness = Dentist with special training who CAN GIVE OPINIONS in court!",
    "summary": "The Dentist as an Expert Witness & Medical Testimony:\n- Ordinary Witness vs Expert Witness:\n  * Ordinary (Fact) Witness: Can testify ONLY to facts personally perceived by their own senses (what they saw, heard, felt); CANNOT give opinions or conclusions.\n  * Expert Witness: A person possessing SPECIAL KNOWLEDGE, skill, experience, training, or education in a particular science, art, or profession;\n    - Exception to the Opinion Rule: An expert witness IS PERMITTED TO GIVE OPINIONS, deductions, and conclusions based on hypothetical questions or scientific evidence presented in court!\n- Role of Dental Expert Witness:\n  * To assist the judge and court in understanding complex medical, dental, and biomechanical evidence.\n  * Must be objective and impartial; Not an advocate for either party.\n  * Evaluates whether the defendant dentist adhered to or breached the recognized 'standard of care' in the specific specialty.\n\nAI Conceptual Breakdown:\nUnder the Rules of Court, opinion evidence is inadmissible because drawing conclusions is the exclusive prerogative of the judge. The Expert Witness is the sole legal exception: because dental diagnosis and surgical technique lie beyond the knowledge of ordinary laypersons, an expert dentist is empowered to interpret radiographs, evaluate surgical technique, and state whether an outcome stemmed from negligence or known biological risk.\n\nPRC Board Pearl:\nDifference between Ordinary and Expert Witness: An Expert Witness is legally permitted to give OPINIONS and conclusions within their field of expertise! Ordinary witnesses can testify only to facts personally perceived.\n\nDr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Ordinary witness = tells what they saw/heard only (NO OPINIONS!).\n* Expert witness = Dentist with special training who CAN GIVE OPINIONS in court!",
