    "pageNumber": 260,
    "title": "Forensic Odontology: Identification & Bite Mark Analysis",
    "subject": "Dental Jurisprudence",
    "day": "Day 3 (11:00 AM \u2022 10%) - Jurisprudence & Ethics",
    "author": "Atty. Marvin Joseph M. Ocampo",
    "keywords": [
      "forensic odontology",
      "disaster victim identification",
      "dvi",
      "bite mark analysis",
      "gustafson method",
      "am pm records"
    ],
    "originalPrint": "Forensic Odontology & Disaster Victim Identification (DVI):\n- Definition: The application of dental science to legal and criminal investigations, primarily for human identification, bite mark analysis, and trauma evaluation.\n- Dental Human Identification:\n  * Teeth and dental restorations are the MOST DURABLE structures in the human body; Highly resistant to post-mortem decomposition, skeletonization, immersion in water, and fire/incineration (enamel withstands up to 1,000\u00b0C).\n  * Primary Identification Method in DVI (Interpol standards):\n    - Comparison of ANTEMORTEM (AM) dental records (charts, radiographs, photos, study casts) with POSTMORTEM (PM) dental autopsy findings.\n    - Unique features: Number of teeth, restorations, missing teeth, root canal fillings, dental implants, anomalies.\n- Bite Mark Analysis:\n  * Bite marks represent human dentition impressions in skin or food; Canine and incisor patterns.\n- Age Estimation (Gustafson's Method - 6 Age Changes in Adult Teeth):\n  1. Attrition; 2. Periodontitis / Gingival attachment level; 3. Secondary Dentin deposition (pulp reduction); 4. Cementum apposition at root; 5. Root resorption; 6. Root Dentin Translucency (most reliable single criterion in older adults!).",
    "aiUnderstanding": "AI Conceptual Breakdown:\nDental identification is definitive because the mathematical permutations of 32 teeth, each possessing 5 anatomical surfaces that can be virgin, restored with various materials, decayed, rotated, or missing, exceeds several billion unique combinations. Secondary dentin apposition and peritubular sclerosis with aging fill dentinal tubules with hydroxyapatite, matching the refractive index of intertubular dentin and making apical root dentin completely transparent (root dentin translucency), providing a quantitative clock for age estimation.",
    "boardPearls": "PRC Board Pearl:\nMost durable biological structures in post-mortem fires: TEETH and dental restorations (withstands up to 1,000\u00b0C)! Identification is achieved by comparing Antemortem (AM) and Postmortem (PM) records. Gustafson's method estimates age using 6 histological tooth changes (root translucency is most reliable).",
    "leaneNotes": "Dr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Teeth withstand up to 1000\u00b0C fire -> #1 for Disaster Victim Identification (DVI)!\n* Compare AM (Antemortem / before death) vs PM (Postmortem / after death) records.\n* Gustafson's method = estimates age from tooth changes (root translucency).",
    "summary": "Forensic Odontology & Disaster Victim Identification (DVI):\n- Definition: The application of dental science to legal and criminal investigations, primarily for human identification, bite mark analysis, and trauma evaluation.\n- Dental Human Identification:\n  * Teeth and dental restorations are the MOST DURABLE structures in the human body; Highly resistant to post-mortem decomposition, skeletonization, immersion in water, and fire/incineration (enamel withstands up to 1,000\u00b0C).\n  * Primary Identification Method in DVI (Interpol standards):\n    - Comparison of ANTEMORTEM (AM) dental records (charts, radiographs, photos, study casts) with POSTMORTEM (PM) dental autopsy findings.\n    - Unique features: Number of teeth, restorations, missing teeth, root canal fillings, dental implants, anomalies.\n- Bite Mark Analysis:\n  * Bite marks represent human dentition impressions in skin or food; Canine and incisor patterns.\n- Age Estimation (Gustafson's Method - 6 Age Changes in Adult Teeth):\n  1. Attrition; 2. Periodontitis / Gingival attachment level; 3. Secondary Dentin deposition (pulp reduction); 4. Cementum apposition at root; 5. Root resorption; 6. Root Dentin Translucency (most reliable single criterion in older adults!).\n\nAI Conceptual Breakdown:\nDental identification is definitive because the mathematical permutations of 32 teeth, each possessing 5 anatomical surfaces that can be virgin, restored with various materials, decayed, rotated, or missing, exceeds several billion unique combinations. Secondary dentin apposition and peritubular sclerosis with aging fill dentinal tubules with hydroxyapatite, matching the refractive index of intertubular dentin and making apical root dentin completely transparent (root dentin translucency), providing a quantitative clock for age estimation.\n\nPRC Board Pearl:\nMost durable biological structures in post-mortem fires: TEETH and dental restorations (withstands up to 1,000\u00b0C)! Identification is achieved by comparing Antemortem (AM) and Postmortem (PM) records. Gustafson's method estimates age using 6 histological tooth changes (root translucency is most reliable).\n\nDr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* Teeth withstand up to 1000\u00b0C fire -> #1 for Disaster Victim Identification (DVI)!\n* Compare AM (Antemortem / before death) vs PM (Postmortem / after death) records.\n* Gustafson's method = estimates age from tooth changes (root translucency).",
