    "originalPrint": "Core Functions of Public Health (IOM Framework):\n- The Three Core Functions of Public Health:\n  1. ASSESSMENT:\n     * Systematically collecting, analyzing, and monitoring health status and community health needs.\n     * Essential Services: Monitor health status to identify community health problems; Diagnose and investigate health hazards in the community.\n  2. POLICY DEVELOPMENT:\n     * Applying scientific knowledge to lead in developing comprehensive public health policies.\n     * Essential Services: Inform, educate, and empower people about health issues; Mobilize community partnerships; Formulate policies and plans that support individual and community health efforts.\n  3. ASSURANCE:\n     * Ensuring that needed health services are available, accessible, and delivered by a competent public health workforce.\n     * Essential Services: Enforce laws and regulations that protect health and ensure safety; Link people to needed personal health services; Assure a competent public health and dental workforce; Evaluate effectiveness, accessibility, and quality of health services.",
    "aiUnderstanding": "AI Conceptual Breakdown:\nThese three core functions operate as a continuous iterative public health cycle. Assessment identifies high dental caries prevalence in school children via epidemiological surveys; Policy Development formulates mandatory fluoride varnish and school toothbrushing programs; Assurance secures funding, trains community health workers, distributes supplies, and evaluates post-intervention DMFT reduction.",
    "boardPearls": "PRC Board Pearl:\nThree Core Functions of Public Health: 1) ASSESSMENT; 2) POLICY DEVELOPMENT; 3) ASSURANCE! Assessment monitors community status; Policy development designs solutions; Assurance guarantees services are delivered by a competent workforce.",
    "leaneNotes": "Dr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* The 3 Core Functions of Public Health:\n  1. ASSESSMENT (find the problem / collect data)\n  2. POLICY DEVELOPMENT (make laws & community programs)\n  3. ASSURANCE (enforce laws & deliver care to people)!",
    "summary": "Core Functions of Public Health (IOM Framework):\n- The Three Core Functions of Public Health:\n  1. ASSESSMENT:\n     * Systematically collecting, analyzing, and monitoring health status and community health needs.\n     * Essential Services: Monitor health status to identify community health problems; Diagnose and investigate health hazards in the community.\n  2. POLICY DEVELOPMENT:\n     * Applying scientific knowledge to lead in developing comprehensive public health policies.\n     * Essential Services: Inform, educate, and empower people about health issues; Mobilize community partnerships; Formulate policies and plans that support individual and community health efforts.\n  3. ASSURANCE:\n     * Ensuring that needed health services are available, accessible, and delivered by a competent public health workforce.\n     * Essential Services: Enforce laws and regulations that protect health and ensure safety; Link people to needed personal health services; Assure a competent public health and dental workforce; Evaluate effectiveness, accessibility, and quality of health services.\n\nAI Conceptual Breakdown:\nThese three core functions operate as a continuous iterative public health cycle. Assessment identifies high dental caries prevalence in school children via epidemiological surveys; Policy Development formulates mandatory fluoride varnish and school toothbrushing programs; Assurance secures funding, trains community health workers, distributes supplies, and evaluates post-intervention DMFT reduction.\n\nPRC Board Pearl:\nThree Core Functions of Public Health: 1) ASSESSMENT; 2) POLICY DEVELOPMENT; 3) ASSURANCE! Assessment monitors community status; Policy development designs solutions; Assurance guarantees services are delivered by a competent workforce.\n\nDr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* The 3 Core Functions of Public Health:\n  1. ASSESSMENT (find the problem / collect data)\n  2. POLICY DEVELOPMENT (make laws & community programs)\n  3. ASSURANCE (enforce laws & deliver care to people)!",
