    "originalPrint": "Microscopic Architecture of Compact (Cortical) Bone:\n- The Osteon (Haversian System):\n  * The basic structural and functional cylindrical unit of mature compact (lamellar) bone, oriented parallel to the long axis of the bone.\n- Components of an Osteon:\n  1. Central (Haversian) Canal:\n     * Longitudinal vascular channel at the center of the osteon; lined by endosteum.\n     * Contains neurovascular bundle (small artery, vein, unmyelinated nerve fibers, and lymphatic vessel).\n  2. Concentric Lamellae:\n     * 4 to 20 concentric cylindrical rings of mineralized bone matrix surrounding the central Haversian canal.\n     * Collagen fibers in adjacent lamellae run in alternating helical directions (herringbone pattern), providing immense resistance to rotational and torsional stress.\n  3. Lacunae:\n     * Small lenticular fluid-filled spaces located at lamellar boundaries; each lacuna contains exactly one mature OSTEOCYTE.\n  4. Canaliculi:\n     * Minute, radiating micro-tunnels traversing the calcified matrix; house osteocyte dendritic cytoplasmic processes.\n     * Connected by gap junctions, permitting diffusion of nutrients, oxygen, and metabolic waste between the central Haversian capillary and distant osteocytes.\n  5. Cement Line (Reversal Line):\n     * Outermost boundary of the osteon; thin, mineral-rich, collagen-poor border that delimits the Haversian system from surrounding matrix; marks the limit of past osteoclastic resorption.\n- Non-Osteonal Bone Structures:\n  * Perforating (Volkmann's) Canals:\n    - Transverse or oblique vascular channels running PERPENDICULAR to the long axis of the bone.\n    - Connect adjacent Haversian canals to each other, to the periosteum externally, and to the marrow cavity internally; NOT surrounded by concentric lamellae.\n  * Interstitial Lamellae: Angular remnants of partially resorbed previous osteons filling spaces between newer osteons.\n  * Circumferential Lamellae: Inner (lines marrow cavity) and Outer (beneath periosteum) lamellae traversing the entire bone circumference.",
    "aiUnderstanding": "AI Conceptual Breakdown:\nUnlike cartilage, which permits nutrient diffusion through its hydrated gel ground substance, mineralized bone matrix is impermeable to water. Bone cells would quickly undergo ischemic necrosis if not for the canalicular-lacunar network. Canaliculi act as micro-plumbing conduits, allowing osteocytes within dense cortical bone to stay alive up to 100 micrometers away from a Haversian blood vessel.",
    "boardPearls": "PRC Board Pearl:\nHaversian canals run LONGITUDINALLY and are surrounded by concentric lamellae! Volkmann's canals run TRANSVERSELY / Perpendicularly and connect Haversian canals together; Volkmann's are NOT surrounded by concentric lamellae. Lacunae house osteocytes; Canaliculi house osteocyte dendritic processes.",
    "leaneNotes": "Dr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* HAVERSIAN canal = Longitudinal (center of osteon, surrounded by rings)!\n* VOLKMANN'S canal = Transverse / Horizontal (cross-connections, NO rings)!\n* Lacunae = Houses the osteocyte!\n* Canaliculi = Mini tunnels with cell arms talking via gap junctions!",
    "summary": "Microscopic Architecture of Compact (Cortical) Bone:\n- The Osteon (Haversian System):\n  * The basic structural and functional cylindrical unit of mature compact (lamellar) bone, oriented parallel to the long axis of the bone.\n- Components of an Osteon:\n  1. Central (Haversian) Canal:\n     * Longitudinal vascular channel at the center of the osteon; lined by endosteum.\n     * Contains neurovascular bundle (small artery, vein, unmyelinated nerve fibers, and lymphatic vessel).\n  2. Concentric Lamellae:\n     * 4 to 20 concentric cylindrical rings of mineralized bone matrix surrounding the central Haversian canal.\n     * Collagen fibers in adjacent lamellae run in alternating helical directions (herringbone pattern), providing immense resistance to rotational and torsional stress.\n  3. Lacunae:\n     * Small lenticular fluid-filled spaces located at lamellar boundaries; each lacuna contains exactly one mature OSTEOCYTE.\n  4. Canaliculi:\n     * Minute, radiating micro-tunnels traversing the calcified matrix; house osteocyte dendritic cytoplasmic processes.\n     * Connected by gap junctions, permitting diffusion of nutrients, oxygen, and metabolic waste between the central Haversian capillary and distant osteocytes.\n  5. Cement Line (Reversal Line):\n     * Outermost boundary of the osteon; thin, mineral-rich, collagen-poor border that delimits the Haversian system from surrounding matrix; marks the limit of past osteoclastic resorption.\n- Non-Osteonal Bone Structures:\n  * Perforating (Volkmann's) Canals:\n    - Transverse or oblique vascular channels running PERPENDICULAR to the long axis of the bone.\n    - Connect adjacent Haversian canals to each other, to the periosteum externally, and to the marrow cavity internally; NOT surrounded by concentric lamellae.\n  * Interstitial Lamellae: Angular remnants of partially resorbed previous osteons filling spaces between newer osteons.\n  * Circumferential Lamellae: Inner (lines marrow cavity) and Outer (beneath periosteum) lamellae traversing the entire bone circumference.\n\nAI Conceptual Breakdown:\nUnlike cartilage, which permits nutrient diffusion through its hydrated gel ground substance, mineralized bone matrix is impermeable to water. Bone cells would quickly undergo ischemic necrosis if not for the canalicular-lacunar network. Canaliculi act as micro-plumbing conduits, allowing osteocytes within dense cortical bone to stay alive up to 100 micrometers away from a Haversian blood vessel.\n\nPRC Board Pearl:\nHaversian canals run LONGITUDINALLY and are surrounded by concentric lamellae! Volkmann's canals run TRANSVERSELY / Perpendicularly and connect Haversian canals together; Volkmann's are NOT surrounded by concentric lamellae. Lacunae house osteocytes; Canaliculi house osteocyte dendritic processes.\n\nDr. Leane's Handwritten Pearls:\n* HAVERSIAN canal = Longitudinal (center of osteon, surrounded by rings)!\n* VOLKMANN'S canal = Transverse / Horizontal (cross-connections, NO rings)!\n* Lacunae = Houses the osteocyte!\n* Canaliculi = Mini tunnels with cell arms talking via gap junctions!",
